---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CommunityLink from "../components/CommunityLink.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <section class="card space-y-4 [&>p]:ml-4">
    <h1 class="text-center">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted text-sm">Last updated: October 27, 2026</p>
    <h3>Introduction</h3>
    <p>
      This policy explains what information the bot collects, how it is used,
      and your rights regarding that information.
    </p>
    <h3>Information We Collect</h3>
    <p>
      <b>Text messages.</b> The content of messages in channels the bot can
      read, both as they are sent and, when a server manager runs /train, from
      the channel history. Only the text is stored, together with the time it
      was stored: not the author, channel or original send time. Mentions inside
      a message are stored as written, so the text can contain Discord user,
      role or channel IDs.
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>Media links.</b> URLs of images, GIFs and videos found in messages or
      attachments, NSFW ones included. The files themselves are not downloaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>Voice.</b> When the bot is in a voice channel (via /vc-join), it
      listens to what is said there and transcribes it into text on our own
      servers. The transcribed text is stored and used like a text message.
      Audio is processed in memory and never stored.
    </p>
    <h3>How We Use Collected Information</h3>
    <p>
      Stored messages and transcripts train a lightweight Markov chain for text
      generation, tied to the server they came from and never shared between
      servers. Media links are posted back by the bot in the same server. Login
      data is used only to show you the servers you manage and let you configure
      them.
    </p>
    <h3>Third Parties</h3>
    <p>
      We do not sell or share any collected data with third parties. Aggregate
      counts (servers, users, voice connections) may be published to bot listing
      sites. Discord itself handles all messages under its own privacy policy.
    </p>
    <h3>Data Storage and Retention</h3>
    <p>
      Each server's data is stored separately on our servers and kept until it
      is deleted. We implement reasonable security measures, but no method of
      transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is 100% secure.
    </p>
    <h3>User Controls and Data Deletion</h3>
    <p>
      Server managers can view, search and delete learned messages and media, or
      clear all of a server's data, from the website (
      <a href="/me">"My servers"</a> dashboard) or with the /wipe command.
      Removing the bot from a server deletes all of that server's data. Anyone
      can also request deletion by contacting us on the <CommunityLink />.
    </p>
    <h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
    <p>
      The bot is not intended for use by individuals under the age of 13. We do
      not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13.
    </p>
    <h3>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h3>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify users
      of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating
      the date above.
    </p>
    <h3>Contact Us</h3>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us on
      the <CommunityLink />.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
